title: Aruba Central Access Point
agents: aruba_central_aps
catalog: hw/network/wlan
license: GPLv2
distribution: checkmk
summary: Monitors one Aruba Central access point on its piggyback host.
description:
 The service evaluates access-point status, sleep status, connected clients,
 CPU utilization, free memory, uptime, firmware, SSID count, model, IP address,
 serial number, MAC address, group, and site.

 Status values other than {Up} are {CRIT} by default. Sleep status is {WARN} by
 default. CPU and free-memory thresholds are configurable, as are optional
 client-count thresholds and a firmware compliance regular expression.

 The piggyback host name is the Aruba Central AP name unless the name is empty
 or equals the MAC address after separator normalization. In that case the
 stable fallback is {AP_<serial>}; a compact MAC is used only when no serial is
 available.
discovery:
 Exactly one service is discovered on each AP piggyback host containing a valid
 {kind=ap} document in the {aruba_central_aps} section.
